/-
# Claim (⋆) for the *old-`rv`* case (Lemmas 3.4 / 3.5 / 3.6) without inverse closure of `S`

Member `m1`, swarm `smw2ngn1z` (direction d5, Lemma 3.8's branch; this file is the companion
observation that the encoding used there also removes a hypothesis from the *other* branch).

## The defect this file repairs

`QE/M5L34_36.lean`'s class form of Claim (⋆) for Lemmas 3.4/3.5/3.6 is
`M5L.ResidualClasses S T` (`∀ y ∈ T, iRV y → ∃ s ∈ S, Cls y s`), and it is proved
(`M5L.ResidualClasses_of_VFGen`) only under the extra hypothesis

> `M5L.VFInvClosedOn S` : every `VF`-element of `S` whose `rv`-class lies in `S` has an inverse
> whose `rv`-class lies in `S`.

`QE/OneStepCases.lean` records why that is a problem: `S`'s `VF`-sort is a sub*ring* of `M` (the
frozen language `L_RV` has **no inverse symbol** on the `VF` sort), so `VFInvClosedOn` does not
follow from `Assembly.Standing S`, and a case hypothesis carrying it is a *strengthening* of the
frozen slot `OneStepVFP`, not a decomposition of it.  In the paper it is free, because
`Ŝ = ⟨VF(S)⟩` is a field with an inverse in `L_v`.

The quotient step is exactly where it is used: `x = p/q` with `rv q ~ rv(c_L)(rv e)^L`, and
`M5L.rvQuotExpansion_mem` inverts `c_L` to obtain `rv x ∈ S`.

## The repair

Do not invert: multiply.  From `rv x · rv q = rv p`, `rv p ~ rv(b_J)(rv e)^J` and
`rv q ~ rv(c_L)(rv e)^L` one gets, multiplying the second relation by `rv x` and transitivity,

> `rv x · rv(c_L · e^L) ~ rv(b_J · e^J)`,

and `c_L·e^L`, `b_J·e^J` are `VF`-elements of `S` (their `rv`-classes are in `S`, because `S` is
closed under `iRVMul` and `rv e ∈ S`).  So the class of `x` is a *ratio* of two classes of `S`,
which is all that `RV(T) ⊆ ⟨RV(S)⟩` needs — the group `⟨RV(S)⟩` contains the inverses internally.

* `RatioInS S y` — the inverse-free statement `y·rv(s) ~ rv(t)` with `s, t ∈ S ∩ VF` nonzero;
* `rvQuotExpansion_ratio` — the quotient step, no `VFInvClosedOn`;
* `ResidualClassesRatio_of_VFGen` — Claim (⋆), old-`rv` branch, from the paper's hypotheses
  (`IsVFGen`, `QuotExpansions`, `M5L.Separated`) **without** `VFInvClosedOn`;
* `ResidualClasses_of_Ratio` — with `VFInvClosedOn` added back, this *implies*
  `M5L.ResidualClasses`, so it is a strict generalisation of the tree's lemma, not a different one;
* `ratio_of_residual` — conversely `M5L.ResidualClasses` implies `RatioInS` when `RV`-elements of
  `S` have `VF` representatives in `S` (`Assembly.IsVFGen S`), so the two forms agree under
  `VFInvClosedOn` + `IsVFGen S`.

No `sorry`, no `axiom`, no `native_decide`; axiom audit at the end.
-/
import M5L34_36

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
set_option maxHeartbeats 1000000

open FirstOrder FirstOrder.Language
open SpecialTransformations.Milestone0
open SpecialTransformations.Milestone0.LRV
open SpecialTransformations.Milestone0.Transfer
open SpecialTransformations.Milestone0.RVCalc
open SpecialTransformations.Milestone0.Transc

namespace SpecialTransformations.Milestone0
namespace M5LOldRV

variable {M : Type} [LRV.Structure M] [hM : M ⊨ Axioms.ACVF]

/-- **`y` lies in the group `⟨RV(S)⟩` generated by the classes of `S`**, written without an inverse:
`y·rv(s)` is class-equal to `rv(t)` with `s, t ∈ S ∩ VF` nonzero.  Multiplying by `rv(s)^{-1}` this
is `y ∈ ⟨RV(S)⟩`; the pair form needs no inverse in `S`. -/
def RatioInS (S : LRV.Substructure M) (y : M) : Prop :=
  ∃ s t : M, iVF s ∧ iVF t ∧ iRv s ∈ S ∧ iRv t ∈ S ∧
    s ≠ iVFZero ∧ t ≠ iVFZero ∧ Transc.Cls (iRVMul y (iRv s)) (iRv t)

/-- **The quotient step without inverse closure.**  `x·q = p` with `p, q` nonvanishing expansions
over `S ∩ VF` and `vv(e)` of infinite order modulo `Γ(S)` gives `RatioInS S (rv x)`. -/
theorem rvQuotExpansion_ratio {S : LRV.Substructure M} {e : M} (he : iVF e) (he0 : e ≠ iVFZero)
    (heS : iRv e ∈ S) (hsep : M5L.Separated S e)
    {b c : ℕ → M} (hb : ∀ i, iVF (b i)) (hbS : ∀ i, b i ∈ S) (hb0 : ∀ i, b i ≠ iVFZero)
    (hc : ∀ i, iVF (c i)) (hcS : ∀ i, c i ∈ S) (hc0 : ∀ i, c i ≠ iVFZero)
    {mM mN : ℕ} {x : M} (hx : iVF x)
    (hq0 : vsum (fun i => iVFMul (c i) (vpow e i)) (mN + 1) ≠ iVFZero)
    (hxq : iVFMul x (vsum (fun i => iVFMul (c i) (vpow e i)) (mN + 1))
      = vsum (fun i => iVFMul (b i) (vpow e i)) (mM + 1)) :
    RatioInS S (iRv x) := by
  set p := vsum (fun i => iVFMul (b i) (vpow e i)) (mM + 1) with hp
  set q := vsum (fun i => iVFMul (c i) (vpow e i)) (mN + 1) with hq
  have hxq' : iVFMul x q = p := by rw [hp, hq]; exact hxq
  have hqVF : iVF q := by
    rw [hq]
    exact iVF_vsum hM (fun i => vf_mul_mem hM (hc i) (iVF_vpow hM he i)) (mN + 1)
  have heRV : iRV (iRv e) := rv_mem hM he
  have hE : ∀ k : ℕ, iRV (rvpow (iRv e) k) := fun k => iRV_rvpow hM heRV k
  have hrvx : iRV (iRv x) := rv_mem hM hx
  have hrvq : iRV (iRv q) := rv_mem hM hqVF
  have hdisB : ∀ i j : ℕ, i ≠ j →
      ¬ Transc.Cls (iRv (iVFMul (b i) (vpow e i))) (iRv (iVFMul (b j) (vpow e j))) := by
    intro i j hij
    rcases Nat.lt_or_gt_of_ne hij with h | h
    · exact M5L.separated_dis hM he he0 hb hbS hb0 hsep h
    · exact fun hc' => M5L.separated_dis hM he he0 hb hbS hb0 hsep h (Transc.cls_symm hc')
  have hdisC : ∀ i j : ℕ, i ≠ j →
      ¬ Transc.Cls (iRv (iVFMul (c i) (vpow e i))) (iRv (iVFMul (c j) (vpow e j))) := by
    intro i j hij
    rcases Nat.lt_or_gt_of_ne hij with h | h
    · exact M5L.separated_dis hM he he0 hc hcS hc0 hsep h
    · exact fun hc' => M5L.separated_dis hM he he0 hc hcS hc0 hsep h (Transc.cls_symm hc')
  obtain ⟨J, -, hJcls⟩ := M5L.cls_vsum_monomial hM he he0 hb hb0 hdisB (m := mM)
  obtain ⟨L, -, hLcls⟩ := M5L.cls_vsum_monomial hM he he0 hc hc0 hdisC (m := mN)
  rw [← hp] at hJcls
  rw [← hq] at hLcls
  have hpv : iRv p = iRVMul (iRv x) (iRv q) := by
    rw [← hxq', rv_mul_hom_of_model hM hx hqVF]
  rw [hpv] at hJcls
  -- multiply `rv q ~ rv(c_L)(rv e)^L` by `rv x`
  have hrs : iRV (iRv (c L)) := rv_mem hM (hc L)
  have huL : iRV (rvpow (iRv e) L) := hE L
  have h1 : Transc.Cls (iRVMul (iRv x) (iRv q))
      (iRVMul (iRv x) (iRVMul (iRv (c L)) (rvpow (iRv e) L))) :=
    Transc.cls_mul_left hM hrvq (rv_mul_mem hM hrs huL) hrvx hLcls
  -- so `rv x · rv(c_L · e^L) ~ rv(b_J · e^J)`
  have hcv : iRv (iVFMul (c L) (vpow e L)) = iRVMul (iRv (c L)) (rvpow (iRv e) L) := by
    rw [rv_mul_hom_of_model hM (hc L) (iVF_vpow hM he L), rv_vpow hM he L]
  have hbv : iRv (iVFMul (b J) (vpow e J)) = iRVMul (iRv (b J)) (rvpow (iRv e) J) := by
    rw [rv_mul_hom_of_model hM (hb J) (iVF_vpow hM he J), rv_vpow hM he J]
  have h2 : Transc.Cls (iRVMul (iRv x) (iRv (iVFMul (c L) (vpow e L))))
      (iRv (iVFMul (b J) (vpow e J))) := by
    rw [hcv, hbv]
    exact Transc.cls_trans hM (rv_mul_mem hM hrvx (rv_mul_mem hM hrs huL))
      (rv_mul_mem hM hrvx hrvq) (rv_mul_mem hM (rv_mem hM (hb J)) (hE J))
      (Transc.cls_symm h1) hJcls
  refine ⟨iVFMul (c L) (vpow e L), iVFMul (b J) (vpow e J), vf_mul_mem hM (hc L) (iVF_vpow hM he L),
    vf_mul_mem hM (hb J) (iVF_vpow hM he J), ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, h2⟩
  · rw [rv_mul_hom_of_model hM (hc L) (iVF_vpow hM he L), rv_vpow hM he L]
    exact M5L.rvMul_mem_sub S (M5L.rv_mem_sub S (hcS L)) (M5L.rvpow_mem_sub S heS L)
  · rw [rv_mul_hom_of_model hM (hb J) (iVF_vpow hM he J), rv_vpow hM he J]
    exact M5L.rvMul_mem_sub S (M5L.rv_mem_sub S (hbS J)) (M5L.rvpow_mem_sub S heS J)
  · exact vf_mul_ne_zero hM (hc L) (iVF_vpow hM he L) (hc0 L) (vpow_ne_zero hM he he0 L)
  · exact vf_mul_ne_zero hM (hb J) (iVF_vpow hM he J) (hb0 J) (vpow_ne_zero hM he he0 J)

/-- **Claim (⋆), old-`rv` branch, without `VFInvClosedOn`**: every `RV`-element of a `VF`-generated
`T` whose `VF`-part is a field of quotients of expansions over `S`, is a ratio of two classes of
`S`. -/
theorem ResidualClassesRatio_of_VFGen {S T : LRV.Substructure M}
    {e : M} (he : iVF e) (he0 : e ≠ iVFZero) (heS : iRv e ∈ S) (hsep : M5L.Separated S e)
    (hVFGen : Assembly.IsVFGen T) (hquot : M5L.QuotExpansions S T e) :
    ∀ y : M, y ∈ T → iRV y → RatioInS S y ∨ y = iRVZero := by
  intro y hyT hyRV
  rcases hVFGen y hyT hyRV with ⟨x, hxT, hxVF, hxr⟩ | hz
  · by_cases hx0 : x = iVFZero
    · right; rw [← hxr, hx0, rv_zero_eq hM]
    · left
      obtain ⟨b, c, mM, mN, hb, hbS, hb0, hc, hcS, hc0, hq0, hxq⟩ := hquot x hxT hxVF hx0
      obtain ⟨s, t, hsVF, htVF, hsRV, htRV, hs0, ht0, hcls⟩ :=
        rvQuotExpansion_ratio he he0 heS hsep hb hbS hb0 hc hcS hc0 hxVF hq0 hxq
      exact ⟨s, t, hsVF, htVF, hsRV, htRV, hs0, ht0, by rw [← hxr]; exact hcls⟩
  · exact Or.inr hz

/-- **`M5L.ResidualClasses` from the ratio form plus `VFInvClosedOn`**: with the extra hypothesis
the tree's lemma assumes, the ratio form gives the tree's conclusion.  So
`ResidualClassesRatio_of_VFGen` is a strict generalisation of `M5L.ResidualClasses_of_VFGen`. -/
theorem ResidualClasses_of_Ratio {S T : LRV.Substructure M} (hfinv : M5L.VFInvClosedOn S) :
    (∀ y : M, y ∈ T → iRV y → RatioInS S y ∨ y = iRVZero) → M5L.ResidualClasses S T := by
  intro h y hyT hyRV
  rcases h y hyT hyRV with ⟨s, t, hsVF, htVF, hsRV, htRV, hs0, ht0, hcls⟩ | hz
  · obtain ⟨s', hs'VF, hs'RV, hss'⟩ := hfinv s hsVF hsRV hs0
    refine ⟨iRv (iVFMul t s'), ?_, rv_mem hM (vf_mul_mem hM htVF hs'VF), ?_⟩
    · rw [rv_mul_hom_of_model hM htVF hs'VF]
      exact M5L.rvMul_mem_sub S htRV hs'RV
    · -- `y·rv s ~ rv t`; multiply by `rv s'` with `rv s · rv s' = 1`
      have hrs : iRV (iRv s) := rv_mem hM hsVF
      have hrs' : iRV (iRv s') := rv_mem hM hs'VF
      have h1 : iRVMul (iRv s) (iRv s') = iRVOne := by
        rw [← rv_mul_hom_of_model hM hsVF hs'VF, hss', rv_one hM]
      have h2 : Transc.Cls (iRVMul (iRVMul y (iRv s)) (iRv s'))
          (iRVMul (iRv t) (iRv s')) :=
        Transc.cls_mul_right hM (rv_mul_mem hM hyRV hrs) (rv_mem hM htVF) hrs' hcls
      have h3 : iRVMul (iRVMul y (iRv s)) (iRv s') = y := by
        rw [rv_mul_assoc_of_model hM hyRV hrs hrs', h1, rv_mul_one_any_right hM hyRV]
      have h4 : iRVMul (iRv t) (iRv s') = iRv (iVFMul t s') :=
        (rv_mul_hom_of_model hM htVF hs'VF).symm
      rwa [h3, h4] at h2
  · exact ⟨iRVZero, M5L.rvZero_mem_sub S, rv_zero_mem hM,
      by rw [hz]; exact Transc.cls_refl hM (rv_zero_mem hM)⟩

/-- **Conversely** `M5L.ResidualClasses` gives the ratio form, provided `RV`-elements of `S` have
`VF` representatives in `S` (`Assembly.IsVFGen S`, which the paper's `Ŝ = ⟨VF(S)⟩` satisfies). -/
theorem ratio_of_residual {S T : LRV.Substructure M} (hVF : Assembly.IsVFGen S)
    (h : M5L.ResidualClasses S T) :
    ∀ y : M, y ∈ T → iRV y → RatioInS S y ∨ y = iRVZero := by
  intro y hyT hyRV
  by_cases hy0 : y = iRVZero
  · exact Or.inr hy0
  · obtain ⟨s, hsS, hsRV, hcls⟩ := h y hyT hyRV
    rcases hVF s hsS hsRV with ⟨t, htS, htVF, hts⟩ | hz
    · have honeVF : iVF (iVFOne (M := M)) := vf_one_mem hM
      have honeRV : iRv (iVFOne (M := M)) ∈ S := by
        rw [rv_one hM]; exact M5L.rvOne_mem_sub S
      have hone0 : iVFOne (M := M) ≠ iVFZero := by
        intro h
        exact rv_one_ne_zero hM (by rw [← rv_one hM, h, rv_zero_eq hM])
      have ht0 : t ≠ iVFZero := by
        intro h
        apply hy0
        have hs0 : s = iRVZero := by rw [← hts, h, rv_zero_eq hM]
        rw [hs0] at hcls
        exact le_infty_eq hM hyRV hcls.2
      have htRV : iRV (iRv t) := rv_mem hM htVF
      refine Or.inl ⟨iVFOne, t, honeVF, htVF, honeRV, M5L.rv_mem_sub S htS, hone0, ht0, ?_⟩
      rw [rv_one hM, rv_mul_one_any_right hM hyRV, hts]
      exact hcls
    · have hs0 : s = iRVZero := hz
      rw [hs0] at hcls
      exact Or.inr (le_infty_eq hM hyRV hcls.2)

/-- **The tree's `M5L.ResidualClasses_of_VFGen` re-derived** from the ratio form (with
`VFInvClosedOn` put back): the two are consistent, and the ratio form is the sharper statement. -/
theorem ResidualClasses_of_VFGen' {S T : LRV.Substructure M}
    {e : M} (he : iVF e) (he0 : e ≠ iVFZero) (heS : iRv e ∈ S) (hsep : M5L.Separated S e)
    (hfinv : M5L.VFInvClosedOn S) (hVFGen : Assembly.IsVFGen T)
    (hquot : M5L.QuotExpansions S T e) :
    M5L.ResidualClasses S T :=
  ResidualClasses_of_Ratio hfinv (ResidualClassesRatio_of_VFGen he he0 heS hsep hVFGen hquot)

/-! ## Axiom audit -/

#print axioms SpecialTransformations.Milestone0.M5LOldRV.rvQuotExpansion_ratio
#print axioms SpecialTransformations.Milestone0.M5LOldRV.ResidualClassesRatio_of_VFGen
#print axioms SpecialTransformations.Milestone0.M5LOldRV.ResidualClasses_of_Ratio
#print axioms SpecialTransformations.Milestone0.M5LOldRV.ratio_of_residual
#print axioms SpecialTransformations.Milestone0.M5LOldRV.ResidualClasses_of_VFGen'

end M5LOldRV
end SpecialTransformations.Milestone0
